From 74fcf8f5421e72b21f5e62d4670cf2450738d9f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:17:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2417/2436] arm64: dts: rockchip: Enable the RK3588 PHP SMMU

Commit cd81d3a0695c ("arm64: dts: rockchip: add rk3588 pcie and php
IOMMUs") added mmu600_php disabled, because nothing programmed the
StreamIDs of its masters. The Rockchip GRF setup now gives GMAC0/1,
SATA0/1/2 and USB3OTG_2 a StreamID each, all six have an iommus
property, and the SMMU has its clock, so enable it.

All six masters share the one TBU of this SMMU and there is no bypass
around it: once the SMMU is enabled, a master without a stream table
entry is aborted. That is why the masters were attached first.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
index 23f5435d5202..0fa6b66b1b8e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
@@ -590,7 +590,6 @@ mmu600_php: iommu@fcb00000 {
 		interrupt-names = "eventq", "gerror", "priq", "cmdq-sync";
 		clocks = <&cru ACLK_MMU_PHP>;
 		#iommu-cells = <1>;
-		status = "disabled";
 	};
 
 	pmu1grf: syscon@fd58a000 {
